          "code": "SUMMARIZE_ANSWER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1766692441298",
          "id": "1766689119567",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766689119568_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou are an analyst preparing a management-ready response for the learning_item_assignments branch. Use the current learning-item–assignments data as the authoritative source and optionally leverage recent chat history and data history to identify the learning item context and maintain continuity.\n\nInputs\n- User question:\n  <user_question>{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}</user_question>\n- Learning-item–assignments data (authoritative):\n  <learning_item_assignments>{{$context.$nodes.GET_DATA_TO_ANSWER_QUERY.$output.output}}</learning_item_assignments>\n- Chat history (system-managed; newest first; may be long or empty):\n  <chat_history>{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}</chat_history>\n- Data history (may be empty/null; JSON that may include learningItemId/learningItemTitle and related fields):\n  <data_history>{{$context.$variables.dataHistory}}</data_history>\n\nScope and data model\n- Records are enrollments for one learning item (preferred) or, if data contains more than one item, a small set of learning items. Fields may include: learningItemTitle/Number/Type, learningFormatMeaning, assignmentType/Meaning (required/voluntary), assignmentStatus/subStatus/Meaning, assignerDisplayName, assignedToDisplayName (learner), assigned/enrolled date, assignmentDueDate, completedDate, expirationDate, assignmentDetailsDeepLink, plus item/worker attributes.\n- Base all statements strictly on learning_item_assignments; do not infer or fabricate missing details.\n\nHistory-aware item context (secondary; never overrides current data)\n- Prefer data_history to resolve item references (e.g., specific learningItemTitle) when that item also appears in current learning_item_assignments.\n- If data_history is missing or insufficient, consult chat_history (newest→oldest) for recent turns where user_intent ∈ { learning_item_assignments, learner_assignments, learner_aggregations, learning_records } that include learningItemId and learningItemTitle.\n- If history is ambiguous, missing, or conflicts with current data, ignore it and rely on current learning_item_assignments only.\n\nInstructions\n- Start with a direct answer to the manager’s question in 1–2 sentences, then provide compact details.\n- Privacy:\n  - Show only names and item details necessary for the item-centric summary.\n  - Do not show emails, person numbers, usernames, or IDs unless explicitly requested and present.\n  - Preserve names and titles exactly as they appear in the data.\n- Status interpretation (values only; no internal keys):\n  - completed = completion date present (or status meaning indicates completion).\n  - overdue = due date in the past AND not completed.\n  - due soon = due date within the next 7 days AND not completed (if due dates exist).\n  - in progress / not started = from status meaning when available; if unclear, omit the detail.\n- Sorting:\n  - Follow explicit user sort requests (e.g., “soonest due first,” “alphabetical”).\n  - Otherwise default to: Overdue, then Due soon, then others; within each group, sort by Learner name (assignedToDisplayName) ascending.\n- Do not display internal schema keys. Use human-readable labels and values only.\n- Omit attributes that are not available; do not include placeholders.\n\nField mappings (values only; omit-if-missing)\n- <Title>: learningItemTitle (plain text; do not hyperlink).\n- <Learner>: assignedToDisplayName (plain text; do not hyperlink).\n- <Status>: human-readable assignment status/substatus meaning (e.g., Overdue, In progress, Not Started, Completed).\n- <Format>: learningFormatMeaning (e.g., Online, Course, Event).\n- <Assigned By>: assignerDisplayName (or “Self Enrolled” when applicable).\n- <Enrolled Date>: assigned/enrolled date (date-only).\n- <Due Date>: due date (date-only).\n- <Completion Date>: completion date (date-only).\n- <Event Date>: session/event date (date-only).\n\nStrict closing rules\n- Do not include suggestions, next steps, offers, or questions unless explicitly requested by the user.\n- End after the requested content (direct answer and the required bullets/totals).\n\nEdge cases\n- No matching records: Output exactly “No relevant enrollments were found for this request.” and end.\n\nRobustness\n- Handle empty/malformed chat_history or data_history gracefully; do not invent items, learners, or attributes.\n- Resolve pronouns/ordinals only if a clear referent exists in data_history or, secondarily, chat_history, and is present in current learning_item_assignments.\n- If contexts conflict, follow the user_question and learning_item_assignments."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Build Incomplete Assignments Payload",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const learningItemId = String($context.$variables.learningItemId || '').trim();\n\nconst result = JSON.stringify({\n  offset: 0,\n  securityFilters: {\n    type: 'MANAGER'\n  },\n  limit: 100,\n  filters: [\n    {\n      name: 'reports',\n      value: 'DIRECT_REPORTS'\n    },\n    {\n      name: 'enrollments',\n      value: 'CURRENT'\n    },\n    {\n      name: 'learningItemId',\n      term: learningItemId\n    }\n  ],\n  sort: [\n    {\n      name: 'assignmentDueDate',\n      direction: 'asc'\n    }\n  ]\n});\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767828302985"
          },
          "code": "BUILD_INCOMPLETE_ASSIGNMENTS_PAYLOAD",
          "id": "1766452929686",
