          "id": "1766441945690",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766441945692_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou are formatting a deterministic panel display for a specific learning item. Do not recompute filtering, due-date classification, sorting, or counts.\n\nInputs\n- User question:\n  <user_question>{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}</user_question>\n- Prepared display model (authoritative):\n  <prepared_display>{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_INCOMPLETE_ASSIGNMENTS_DISPLAY.$output.result}}</prepared_display>\n\nAuthoritative rules\n- Treat prepared_display as the source of truth.\n- prepared_display.rows is already filtered to overdue-or-due-within-30-days records and already sorted.\n- prepared_display.totalFiltered, overdueCount, dueSoonCount, and asOfDate are already computed.\n- Use row.learnerName exactly as provided.\n- Use row.dueDate exactly as provided.\n- Use row.statusText exactly as provided.\n- Apply a badge only on the Status cell:\n  - row.statusKey = overdue -> priority \"alert\", badgeText \"Overdue\"\n  - row.statusKey = dueSoon -> priority \"warning\", badgeText \"Due within 30 days\"\n\nOutput format\n- Output order:\n  1) One panel title line\n  2) One subtitle line\n  3) The multiRecordWidget JSON payload for the table\n- No extra prose.\n\nTitle and subtitle\n- If prepared_display.totalFiltered > 0:\n  - Title: \"{N} assignments: {O} overdue, {D} due within 30 days\"\n- Else:\n  - Title: \"No incomplete assignments for this item\"\n- Subtitle:\n  - \"Prioritized by urgency • Updated <YYYY-MM-DD>\" using prepared_display.asOfDate\n\nTable\n- Use a multiRecordWidget with cols: [\"Learner\", \"Due Date\", \"Status\"]\n- Emit one row per object in prepared_display.rows using this order:\n  - Learner: learnerName\n  - Due Date: dueDate\n  - Status: statusText with the badge mapping above\n- If there are no rows, emit a multiRecordWidget with the specified columns and zero rows."
            }
          ],
