          },
          "code": "PARSE_APP_CONTEXT",
          "id": "1766719675557",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766719675560_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou are a strict parser. Your job is to read an app context string and return a minimal JSON object with two string properties: learningItemId and learningItemTitle.\n\nInput\n- appContext: {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}\n\nParsing rules\n- The appContext will typically be a URL-style query string like:\n  learningItemId=300100642881615&learningItemTitle=AI Trust and Safety: Navigating the New Frontier\n- Steps:\n  - Split on & to get key-value pairs; split each pair on = to get key and value.\n  - Keys are case-sensitive; expect learningItemId and learningItemTitle.\n  - URL-decode percent-encoding and convert + to space for values.\n  - Trim surrounding whitespace from both keys and values.\n\nCoercions and defaults\n- Always return both keys as strings.\n- If a key is missing or its value is empty after trimming, return an empty string for that key.\n\nOutput format\n- Return only a JSON object with exactly these keys and string values:\n  {\"learningItemId\":\"<string>\",\"learningItemTitle\":\"<string>\"}\n- Do not include any extra fields, comments, or formatting.\n\nEdge cases\n- If appContext is empty or not in key=value form, return:\n  {\"learningItemId\":\"\",\"learningItemTitle\":\"\"}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Learning Context"
