          "code": "RENDER_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1767913857270",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767913857277_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou generate a concise 1–2 sentence summary for a specific learning item using a deterministic prepared display model. Do not recompute filtering, due-within-30-days status, overdue status, or counts.\n\nInputs\n- Prepared display model (authoritative):\n  <prepared_display>{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_INCOMPLETE_ASSIGNMENTS_DISPLAY.$output.result}}</prepared_display>\n\nAuthoritative rules\n- Use prepared_display.totalFiltered as N.\n- Use prepared_display.overdueCount as O.\n- Use prepared_display.dueSoonCount as D.\n- Use prepared_display.asOfDate exactly as provided.\n- If a next due date is needed, use the first row in prepared_display.rows whose statusKey is dueSoon.\n\nOutput requirements\n- Produce 1–2 plain sentences, no bullets, quotes, labels, or extra whitespace.\n- Do not include emails, person numbers, or internal IDs.\n\nContent rules\n1) If N = 0:\n   - \"No incomplete assignments for this item in the next 30 days. All clear as of <YYYY-MM-DD>.\"\n2) If O > 0:\n   - \"<N> incomplete assignments for this item; <O> overdue. <D> due within 30 days.\"\n   - If D > 0 and a due-within-30-days row exists, optionally append: \"Next due <YYYY-MM-DD>.\"\n3) Else:\n   - \"<N> incomplete assignments for this item; all due within 30 days. Next due <YYYY-MM-DD>.\"\n\nFormatting\n- Dates: YYYY-MM-DD.\n- Numbers: integers.\n- Do not exceed two sentences total."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Add Data To History",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const maxSize = 3;\n\nconst storeKey = ['data', 'Hist', 'ory'].join('');\nconst rawStore = $context.$variables[storeKey];\nconst runData = ($context.$nodes.GET_DATA_TO_ANSWER_QUERY.$output.output ?? null);\n\nconst state = (rawStore && typeof rawStore === \"object\" && Array.isArray(rawStore.records))\n  ? { runCount: Number(rawStore.runCount) || rawStore.records.length, records: rawStore.records.slice() }\n  : (Array.isArray(rawStore)\n      ? { runCount: rawStore.length, records: rawStore.slice() }\n      : { runCount: 0, records: [] });\n\nconst record = {\n  timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n  runData\n};\n\nstate.records.push(record);\nwhile (state.records.length > maxSize) state.records.shift();\n\nstate.runCount = (Number(state.runCount) || 0) + 1;\n\nreturn state;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766689119567"
          },
          "code": "ADD_DATA_TO_HISTORY",
